window.products.push({"id":148441,"name":"Whirlpool WP8318084 Washer Lid Switch Kenmore Maytag Washing Machine Assembly Door Part AP6012742 PS11745957 LSR5132PQ1 MVWC300VW1 WTW5540SQ0 ITW4300S","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":9.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61vbdLblbzL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Washer Door Switch 8318084 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers WP8318084 AP6012742, ES8084, PS11745957, TJ90ES8084, WP8318084VP. Wp8318084 Lid Switch is compatible with Whirlpool, Admiral, Amana, Crosley, Estate, Inglis, Kenmore, KitchenAid, Magic Chef, Maytag, Roper. Lid Switch Wp8318084 is an essential component of the washing machine's safety system and is responsible for preventing the washer from operating while the lid is open. Green grounding wire included. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Pn 8318084? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Whirlpool 8318084 Lid Switch For Washer will help if your appliance does not start, does not agitate, the timer does not advance, or it pumps but does not spin. Installing the Whirlpool Lid Switch 8318084 in a washer is a simple process that can be completed in a few steps. 💡 Whirlpool Lid Switch Wp8318084 is located under the lid of the washer and is activated when the lid is closed. When the lid is closed, the switch sends a signal to the washer's control board, allowing it to start the wash cycle. If the lid is open or the switch is malfunctioning, the control board will not receive the signal and the washer will not start. Washer Lid Switch 8318084 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 What is the difference between lid lock and lid switch? They are two different components used in washing machines to prevent the machine from operating while the lid is open. A lid switch detects when the lid is closed and sends a signal to the control board to start the wash cycle, while a lid lock physically locks the lid in place to prevent it from being opened during the wash cycle. Both components are important for ensuring the safe and proper operation of a washing machine. 💡 Is it possible to bypass the Lid Switch? While it may be technically possible to bypass the lid switch, doing so is not recommended as it could be dangerous and may cause damage to the appliance. By bypassing the lid switch, you could potentially expose yourself to electric shock or injury from moving parts. Additionally, if the appliance continues to run with the lid open, it could cause damage to the appliance itself or to your surroundings.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61vbdLblbzL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07V5X6RF8","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-148441","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07V5X6RF8","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07V5X6RF8","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
