window.products.push({"id":148803,"name":"W10120998 Dryer Lint Screen Replacement Maytag AP3967919 MGDB765FW0 WED7500GC0 MED7230HW2 WED8127LW1 MED6230HW0 MEDB765FW0 MEDE500VW1 MEDX500XW0 WED55","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":14.25,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81AdOwJus5S._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Dryer Lint Screen W10120998 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP3967919, 1206293, 3390721, 8066170, 8572268, AH1491676, EA1491676, PS1491676, W10049370, W10120998VP, W10178353, W10596627. Lint Filter W10120998 is compatible with a big amout of brands. Dryer Lint Filter W10120998 is made of durable materials and features a fine mesh screen that efficiently captures lint. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Dryer Lint Filter W10120998 will help if your appliance takes too long to dry, there's no heat or not enough heat, it shuts off too soon, there are marks left on clothes. It is recommended to clean the Dryer Lint Filter W10120998 periodically to ensure optimal performance. 💡 The purpose of the W10120998 Dryer Lint Screen Filter Replacement is to capture lint and debris from clothes during the drying process, preventing them from accumulating in the dryer and potentially causing a fire hazard. W10120998 Filter fits hundreds of models and can be easily installed in just a few minutes with basic DIY repair skills. Our Lint Screen W10120998 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Why does so much lint get past the lint trap? Even if the lint trap in your dryer is working correctly, it is possible for lint to accumulate in the exhaust duct or vent. This can happen due to poor airflow caused by clogs or obstructions in the exhaust system, a low-quality lint trap that becomes less effective over time, certain fabric types that shed more lint, and overloading the dryer. To avoid lint buildup, clean and maintain the W10120998 Dryer Lint Filter and exhaust system regularly. 💡 What happens if you don't remove the lint? If you don't remove lint from your dryer's lint trap and exhaust system, it can lead to a variety of problems, including reduced dryer efficiency, longer drying times, increased energy consumption, higher utility bills, and potentially even a fire hazard. Lint buildup can restrict airflow, cause the dryer to overheat, and increase the risk of a dryer fire. Clean and maintain your lint trap and exhaust system regularly to prevent these issues.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81AdOwJus5S._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07VV4B4VJ","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-148803","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07VV4B4VJ","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07VV4B4VJ","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
